## This is a greenfield build that harvests requirements
Six HTML tools are being RETIRED, not ported. No code is reused and no output of
them is a target — OD B1 is CLOSED. They are read-only evidence in
docs/requirements/, and an extract there is never current truth.

Acceptance is four standards, by domain. No evidence means FAIL.
- Money & quantity — exact match against the signed worked examples in
  CALC_SPEC.md. Zero drift. A rounding rule is stated per calculation. Legacy
  numbers are not a reference: no tax, no freight, no money rounding exists in
  the retiring tools.
- Print — the measured physical tolerance in PRINT_CONTRACT.md, plus
  byte-identical PrintArtifact output across platforms (OD-E11). Legacy
  printouts are not a reference.
- Features & entities — conformance to FEATURE_INVENTORY.md and DOMAIN_MODEL.md.
- Tenant isolation — proof that tenant A cannot read tenant B, on every gate
  touching data access. Not waivable by OD.

Legacy defects are requirements the new build must not reproduce (OD B3), listed
in FEATURE_INVENTORY.md. Never edit a file under legacy/.

## Returns are the highest-risk logic in this product
Returns affect net revenue, COGS, product summary, Component usage, monthly
profit, StockLevel, and every report. Returns are StockMovement records with
reason return_restock or return_writeoff (OD-C3); their money effect is a
CreditNote — an issued Invoice is immutable, and outstanding equals
Invoice − Payments − CreditNotes (OD-C16).

Anything touching returns is heavyweight, full ceremony, with tests covering at
minimum: a partial return, a full return, both dispositions, and both legacy
outAllocations shapes.

Two live divergences must be settled, not inherited: unmarked dispositions
default in opposite directions across the two retiring tools, and returns were
valued at list price against a discounted invoice total. Neither is a target.
Both are decisions for DOMAIN_MODEL.md and CALC_SPEC.md.

## Model class
Heavyweight: architecture · storage layer · print engine · document rendering ·
template engine · CSV importer · returns/COGS/profit math · BrandConfig schema ·
every exit-verification gate · anything touching tenant isolation, regardless of
size.
Standard: UI wiring, forms, tests, land tasks, CRUD on specified entities.

## Design boundary
The shared component library belongs to the design surface; its location is
fixed at Gate 3. Compose and wire; never restyle. Token-only styling. Gaps
route back to design.

## Every session ends the same way
Four files, in order: (1) SESSION_CONTEXT.md — done-steps row, phase, last
task, verdict, next action, open-id list; (2) docs/method/CARRY_FORWARDS.md —
land/amend/close rows, never close without explicit authorisation; (3)
docs/method/PRECEDENTS.md — append any new ruling or environment quirk, never
rewrite an existing entry; (4) DEVELOPMENT_JOURNAL.md — append one line:
Date | Model | Phase/Task | Files | Issues | Next

## Report honestly
State deviations from the canonical prompt and why, done-when criteria you
could not meet, and carry-forwards discovered. Never put credentials in any
chat surface.

## Stack
Withheld until Gate 3. Architecture, framework, layering and folder structure
are deliberately undecided; they are authored in ARCHITECTURE.md and its ADRs
after the prepare phase closes. Do not infer one, and do not add a dependency.

Three constraints are fixed by signed decisions and are not open: PWA client
with an online database on Supabase (G4) · hosted on Vercel (G9) · per-tenant
private data with database isolation (G3).

If a task appears to require a stack decision, stop and flag it.
